c Graph H_10 of Theorem 1 in 'The CLIQUES Algorithm Is Not Output-Polynomial' (Sec. 3)
c target n = 300; nearest H_k has n = 2k^2+9k = 290 vertices (k = 10)
c maximal cliques: 2861 (Lemma bound (k+1)(2k(k+3)+1) = 2871 <= n^2 = 84100)
c every run of CLIQUES makes at least 2^(k+1)-1 = 2047 recursive calls (one run with min-label tie-breaking and increasing order: 39921)
c vertices: guards g_i = 1..10; core a_i = k+2i-1, b_i = k+2i (11..30); witnesses 31..290, 13 per core vertex in the order a_1, b_1, a_2, ...
p edge 290 7910
